          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तलवार",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तलवार — talvār — \"a sword\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "राजा ने तलवार उठाई। rājā ne talvār uṭhāī. The king raised his sword."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तलवार (talvār) goes back to Sanskrit taravāri, \"a sword\" (CDIAL 5706), which CDIAL gives with a Hindi talwār. It is feminine: तलवार उठाई."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
